## Contract and implementation

1. Init never installs a remote push mapping. On the selected existing remote, normal and force init remove all local values exactly equal to `refs/etude/*:refs/etude/*`. Use exact matching and Git's config lock/retry support; preserve every other value byte-for-byte and in order. No trimming or semantic equivalence for ownership. The literal is an ownership heuristic, not proof: document removal even if a user intentionally set that same local value.
2. Only local configuration is eligible for migration. Preserve system/global/included policies, other remotes, push.default, upstream and branch policies. Do not manufacture a heads refspec to counter inherited mappings. Test scoped config using disposable GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM/GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL files; never edit real global settings. Inherited canonical values remain user policy and may still affect push. Inspect include handling so preview does not promise removal of entries it cannot edit.
3. Preserve hazardous-fetch cleanup order/semantics and safe sibling mirror fetching. Force retains existing behavior of not adding mirror mappings, while performing both legacy cleanups. Preserve missing-remote normal/explicit/force outcomes. Dry-run is write-free and accurately previews push removals on both paths and the existing supported fetch actions.
4. Replace missing-push warnings with explicit metadata-publication guidance (`etude sync`). Doctor must accept absent/partial metadata push coverage: sync supplies its own explicit refspec. Preserve doctor validation of configured invalid mappings and mirror-push hazards. No unrelated doctor redesign.
5. Sync continues explicit non-forced refs/etude transfer; branch pushing follows Git user policy. Sibling mirror refs must not be uploaded by sync.

